{{!-- The reading column's body, in whichever state the platform put it.

THE BODY'S ACCESS BRANCH LIVES HERE. Both layouts call this partial, so the Gate cannot be
reachable from one of them and not the other, and there is no second copy of the article-or-Gate
decision to fall behind the first. Everything above this — the cover or the title page, the
standfirst, the byline — is the same in both states, which is the point: the Gate is a state of
one Post, not a Layout and not a Surface of its own.

Two other places read `access`, and both are the same decision about the contents list rather
than about the body: `post/a1.hbs` guards its inline disclosure and `post/rail.hbs` guards A2's
rail list. They are separate because the two layouts hang that list in different places, and
rail.hbs carries the reasoning for both.

WHY THIS DOES NOT CALL {{content}} ON THE GATED BRANCH. Ghost's content helper substitutes its
own `gh-post-upgrade-cta` panel for the body whenever `access` is false, and takes no option to
stop it — the panel is the helper's return value, not something appended after it. So the gated
branch prints `html` directly. That is not a hole in the gate: Ghost's output serializer has
already replaced `html` with the free portion before any template runs (the part before the
post's paywall card, or the empty string when there is none), so the triple-stash cannot reach
a word the reader has not been given. It is also why the free portion needs no clipping.

The design clips that teaser to 150px and fades it into the card. That is not ported, and the
reason is the same one that says a photograph must not be cropped: the free portion is the part
the author chose to publish, and hiding it behind a gradient with no way to open it is the
theme deciding to withhold something the platform gave away. The fade only means anything above
a clip, so it goes with it. Recorded as a Concession.

The tags row goes with the body because it closes the article — the design's own source keeps
"Filed under" inside the body component, so a gated post shows the chips no more than it shows
the last chapter. What stays is everything below the article: the share row, the writer, the
neighbours, the related posts, the subscribe band. --}}
{{#if access}}
	<div class="mirror-content">{{content}}</div>

	{{> "post/tags"}}
{{else}}
	{{#if html}}
		<div class="mirror-content">{{{html}}}</div>
	{{/if}}

	{{> "post/gate"}}
{{/if}}
